# One more thing: don't build a "LangChain agent" and then put LangGraph around it blindly

A common mistake is:

```text
LangGraph
   ↓
LangChain Agent
   ↓
LangGraph
   ↓
LangChain Tool
   ↓
Agent
```

and suddenly nobody knows who controls what.

Our architecture should have a clear hierarchy:

```text
                 LANGGRAPH
             Workflow Authority
                     │
          ┌──────────┴──────────┐
          │                     │
   Deterministic Nodes     Specialist Agent
          │                     │
          │                LANGCHAIN
          │              Agent/Tool Layer
          │                     │
          │                 MCP Client
          │                     │
          └──────────┬──────────┘
                     ▼
              MCP TOOL LAYER
                     │
                     ▼
              PROVIDER ADAPTER
                     │
                     ▼
               PROVIDER API
```

**LangGraph owns orchestration.**

**LangChain helps construct the agent.**

**MCP controls external tool access.**

**Provider adapters control external integrations.**

**Deterministic services control money, ranking, security and verification.**

That's the architecture I would use.

