## So, yes: Phase 1 uses both

| Technology                | Phase 1? | Job                                        |
| ------------------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------ |
| **LangGraph**             | ✅ YES    | Main Shopping workflow/orchestration       |
| **LangChain**             | ✅ YES    | Shopping Agent + tool/LLM layer            |
| **MCP**                   | ✅ YES    | Controlled provider tool interface         |
| **Shopping Agent**        | ✅ YES    | Complex shopping reasoning                 |
| **Recommendation Engine** | ✅ YES    | Deterministic ranking                      |
| **Payment Intelligence**  | ✅ YES    | Deterministic monetary optimization        |
| **Provider Adapters**     | ✅ YES    | Amazon/Flipkart/etc. integration isolation |
| **A2A**                   | ❌ NO     | Future external-agent collaboration        |
| Multi-agent swarm         | ❌ NO     | Unnecessary for Phase 1                    |
| Autonomous purchasing     | ❌ NO     | Future                                     |

So your Antigravity prompt **already had the correct high-level architecture**, but I would absolutely add the above section. Otherwise a coding agent could interpret "LangChain + LangGraph" too loosely and build a generic agent loop rather than the controlled architecture we actually want.
